  "plain": "No rule is calibrated. The rule the plan selected, `rel`, changes the sign of its implied scale across the four pairs and predicts -0.000251 for the reallocation against a measured +0.000366 \u2014 which is exactly why the error-driven build lost. `numel` also gets that sign wrong. `abs` and `sqrt_energy` get the sign right on all four pairs, but out of sample they are off by up to 4.4x and 2.5x respectively, and their implied scale spreads 13.3x and 2.5x across the pairs. A rule that is a factor of two-and-a-half uncertain cannot decide a 1e-4 fidelity claim, so there is no surrogate here good enough to authorise a conversion on prediction alone. `sqrt_energy` is the least-bad and is the pre-registrable candidate for a next attempt; its selection must be validated on a BETWEEN-role reallocation delta, which is the test the rank-9 rule lacked."
 }
